TX: /dev/serial/by-id/usb-1a86_USB2.0-Ser_-if00-port0 -> /dev/ttyUSB0; RX: /dev/serial/by-id/usb-SIPEED_UARTx4_HS_FactoryAIOT_Prog_Serial-if00 -> /dev/ttyACM0
921600 baud, 8N1, both endpoints pre-set. Physical TX/RX wiring and no RTS/CTS wiring.
The account shell uses isolated fish configuration. Both limited cases use soft flow and the default 500 ms exit wait. The 128 KiB limited case resumes at 50% occupancy. The zero-queue case paces at 99% of the configured link byte rate and has no watermarks.
File sizes use 1024 B per KiB; numbered ASCII rows are exactly 128 file bytes each (127 text + LF). Expected RX includes CRLF and the cat/exit prompts. exit timeouts are milliseconds, -1 means unlimited.
Timing uses monotonic user-space observation: cat send to final local file byte; RX first to last observed byte, even when truncated; queue wait from interactive shell pidfd ready to queue empty/deadline notice. The shell exit observation can differ slightly from the program's internal exit start. Reception continues until both process exit and 0.5 s of RX silence. Zero-queue near-zero exit latency is overhead, not a positive drain time.
Flow cycles are distinct pause/resume notices, with periodic updates grouped. Pause duration is between observed notices. Payload counts during/after pause exclude program notices; after=0 can mean the file already ended. Active paced KiB/s excludes observed watermark pauses and measures the remaining first-to-last local payload span.
Details below: one CASE JSON record per attempt; no values estimated for rejected runs.

